c DIMACS CNF: the format every SAT solver eats.
c   p cnf <#vars> <#clauses>, then one clause per line, literals
c   space-separated and 0-terminated. Negation is a minus sign.
c
c This encodes: (x1 or x2) and (not x1 or x3) and (not x3).
c   z3 learning/solver/sat.cnf   ->   sat -1 2 3
c i.e. x1=false, x2=true, x3=false.
c
c Add the clause "-2 0" (x2 must be false) and it becomes UNSATISFIABLE:
c that is what a *proved* property looks like at this layer.
p cnf 3 3
1 2 0
-1 3 0
-3 0
